        "content": "A study published in 2020 examined potential foreign markets for Iranian sporting goods using United Nations secondary data. Its abstract reports that two analytical approaches produced different preferred destinations. This matters because an attractive market identified by a model is an analytical result, rather than evidence that Iranian suppliers subsequently entered that market or increased sales there. [s1]\n\nThe authors identified sanctions, inflation, exchange-rate fluctuations, political instability, and national branding as obstacles. These are findings from that historical study, not a verified description of every manufacturer’s circumstances at the editorial cutoff. Only the abstract was accessible for this page; detailed product classifications, calculations, and underlying trade observations were not inspected. Consequently, no export rankings, annual values, or present-day market recommendations are reproduced here. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "governance-and-branches",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Organizations, commercial relationships, and evidence",
        "content": "The Asian Football Confederation, the regional governing body for Asian football, treats commercial development as part of club development. Its 2026 licensing regulations include marketing alongside sporting, infrastructure, personnel, legal, financial, and sustainability criteria. This establishes the breadth of the regulatory framework; it does not establish that individual Iranian clubs satisfy every requirement. [s2]\n\nThe branches below explore different questions. Club management concerns organizational responsibility and eligibility. Sports marketing concerns relationships with audiences and sponsors. Sportswear and equipment concern goods, while sports media and athlete performance analytics require their own evidence about rights, services, and operational use. These distinctions organize this guide; they are not a statistical classification of Iran’s economy.",
        "source_ids": ["s2"]
      }
